.SH "NAME"
pcre2_substring_get_byname \- extract named substring into new memory
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_substring_get_byname\fP\f(CR(pcre2_match_data *\fP\f(CImatch_data\fP\f(CR,
                               PCRE2_SPTR\fP \f(CIstringname\fP\f(CR,
                               PCRE2_UCHAR **\fP\f(CIstringptr\fP\f(CR,
                               PCRE2_SIZE *\fP\f(CIsizeptr\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This is a convenience function for extracting a captured substring by name into
newly acquired memory. The arguments are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 11
\f(CImatch_data\fP
.ad l
The match data for the match
.TP 11
\f(CIstringname\fP
.ad l
Name of the required substring
.TP 11
\f(CIstringptr\fP
.ad l
Where to put the string pointer
.TP 11
\f(CIsizeptr\fP
.ad l
Where to put the string length
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The memory in which the substring is placed is obtained by calling the same
memory allocation function that was used for the match data block. The
convenience function \f(CBpcre2_substring_free()\fP can be used to free it when
it is no longer needed. The yield of the function is zero for success or one of
the following error numbers:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING\fP
.ad l
there are no groups of that name
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE\fP
.ad l
the ovector was too small for that group
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_UNSET\fP
.ad l
the group did not participate in the match
.TP 24
\f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY\fP
.ad l
memory could not be obtained
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
If there is more than one group with the given name, the first one that is set
is returned. In this situation \f(CBPCRE2_ERROR_UNSET\fP means that no group with the
given name was set.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.